## Why Most Rows Are Blank

- **Total GWP** of **₹1,357 crore** and **Retail health GWP** of **₹768 crore** are the only line items with a confirmed, sourceable Q1FY26 value — pulled from the Aditya Birla Capital Q2 FY26 investor deck's Health Insurance segment table, on the statutory (1/n) basis.
- **NWP, NEP, EoM ratio, and Net worth** all require the IRDAI statutory "NL" return set (NL-1 Revenue Account, NL-2 expense schedule, NL-3 Balance Sheet) for the quarter ended 30 June 2025. This filing is not indexed or hosted anywhere publicly locatable as of the current date — the ABHI disclosure page only carries a legacy December 2016 NL set.
- **Claims ratio, expense ratio, commission ratio, combined ratio, and solvency ratio** are not disclosed in either the investor presentation or any retrievable statutory document for this period.
- **PAT (IGAAP or IFRS)** is not separately broken out — the only profitability metric shown in the available source is **Profit Before Tax**, reported as **-₹36 crore** (without 1/n adjustment) / **-₹24 crore** (with 1/n adjustment), not PAT.
- **Retail health market share** is disclosed only on a cumulative **H1FY26** basis (**13.6%** vs. prior-year **11.9%**, on a Sales-GWP basis) — not isolated to Q1 alone, so it was left blank rather than mixing periods.
- **AUM and investment yield** are not disclosed at the ABHI segment level in any retrievable Q1FY26 document.

## Recommendation

To close the remaining data gaps (NWP, NEP, EoM ratio, Net worth, all ratios, AUM, investment yield, and standalone PAT), the Q1FY26 IRDAI "NL" statutory return set would need to be sourced either:
1. Directly from the IRDAI portal's insurer-wise public disclosure repository (in case ABHI's compliance team has re-hosted the filing under a different URL path than the one referenced), or
2. Via a direct request to Aditya Birla Capital's Investor Relations desk, since the filing does not currently appear to be indexed by public search engines or hosted on the company's own disclosure page.</ans>
